BOARD A'S FRONT-END CURRENT-LIMIT RESISTOR R11: THE HELD CIRCUIT AND THE PROPOSED CHANGE (r11_dep.py, stream r11dep,
MESHSAT-1357). PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing built, powered or measured; no generator edited; no requirement changed.
Basis per figure: MAKER (page), NETLIST, MODELED, INFERRED (method stated), ASSUMPTION (a figure no document gives).

1. THE CIRCUIT (NETLIST v2/ecad/pcb-a-power-a23/out/pcb-a-power.net, sha256/16 6c40250c47195ebb; board E v2/ecad/pcb-e1-dock-e7/out/pcb-e1-dock.net, sha256/16 2ed95a0e8069ebf8)
   R11 10mOhm 1% 2512 (ISNS) from FE_OUT to VBUS20: the LM5176 U2's AVERAGE (ISNS) current sense, in series with its OUTPUT
   ISNS filter R160, R161 100R 1% and C128 1n into U2 pins 14 and 13; R12 5mOhm 1% 2512 is the cycle-by-cycle CS resistor
   L1 10uH XAL1010-103ME (Isat 17.5 A); Q2 to Q5 CSD19532Q5B 100 V N-FET
   VIN_RAW: C11, C12 10u 100V X7R 1210; J_VR1 to J_VR4 '9 A spring pin, VIN_RAW'; no fuse on board A's VIN_RAW
   VBUS20: 6 x EEHZK1V331P bulk (C163, C178, C179, C180, C199, C200); U2's BIAS (pin 24) on VBUS20, so its supply current passes R11
   MODE: R119 to VCC (no hiccup, SNVSAI1D p.20); SLOPE C147 680p; SS C7 4.7u; RT R8 40.2k (206 kHz)
   the taps: ISNS(+) U2.14 on FE_ISNS_P through R160 from FE_OUT ('Kelvin from the shunt's output pad'); ISNS(-) U2.13 on FE_ISNS_N through R161 from
     VBUS20 ('Kelvin from the shunt's rail pad'); CS U2.16 through R150 from FE_CS, CSG U2.15 through R151 from GND. A netlist names the net a tap
     lands on, not the point on it: it states the Kelvin intent and can neither establish nor refute the connection. The
     current netlist shows NO tap error; the Kelvin connection is a LAYOUT property of a board this netlist does not yet have
   board E's VIN_RAW sources: the vehicle entry (F1 '10 A mini blade (Keystone 3568 holder)', LM5069 U6) and the panel tracker (LT8705A, R5 '5 mOhm 1% 3 W 2512 RSENSE', L1 '10uH Coilcraft XAL1510-103MED'),
   ORed through the ideal diode U4 with Q2 'BSC039N06NS 60 V 3.9 mOhm N-FET'; the panel input F2 '10 A mini blade (Keystone 3568 holder)'
   facts: 14 of 14 hold

2. THE PARTS AND THE MAKERS' FIGURES
   R11 held: C2903468 (lcsc_fill.py); LCSC's answer (v2/docs/records/r11dep/inputs/lcsc-C2903468-2026-09-30.json): Milliohm HoJLR2512-3W-10mR-1%, 3W, ±1% (read 2026-09-30T01:19Z)
   HoJLR2512 series (MAKER, v2/vendor/passives/milliohm-hojlr2512-series.pdf, sha256/16 3224518dbc8bdc85): 2512, 3 W for 0.5 to 500 mOhm (p.1); TCR +-50 ppm/K for 2 to 500 mOhm;
     -50 to +170 C, derated linearly from 70 C (100 %) to 170 C (0 %) (p.2); rated current sqrt(P/R) (p.3); short-time
     overload 5 x rated power for 5 s, load life 1000 h at rated power and 70 C, each within +-1 % (p.4)
   R11 proposed: 6.2 mOhm (energy_two_pack.py fe_r11_draft_mohm; a1elec CHARGER.md 2), rated here as the same series,
     HoJLR2512-3W-6.2mR-1% by the maker's own part-number scheme (p.1): the value lies in its 3 W range; ORDER CODE NOT
     ESTABLISHED (no catalogue answer read for it)
   LM5176 (MAKER, v2/vendor/ti/lm5176-datasheet.pdf): VSNS 43 / 50 / 57 mV over TJ -40 to 125 C (p.7), ICL(AVG) = 50 mV / RSNS (Equation 4, p.17),
     ISNS pin bias 3 uA TYPICAL (p.7, no limit printed), ISNS common mode 0 to 55 V (p.5), CC loop gm 1 mS into SS (p.7),
     boost peak 100 / 120 / 140 mV and buck valley 66 / 80 / 94 mV on CS (p.7), fSW 175 / 200 / 225 kHz at RT 40 k (p.6)
   U3 BQ25731 (MAKER, v2/vendor/ti/bq25731-datasheet.pdf): IIN_HOST 6.2 A set; its maximum 6.355 A, the larger of the 100 mA of p.80 and the +-2.5 % of p.1
   L1 XAL1010-103ME (MAKER, v2/vendor/power/coilcraft-xal1010.pdf p.1): 10 uH +-20 %, DCR 13.40 / 14.75 mOhm, Isat 17.5 A (30 % drop, typical, 25 C),
     Irms 11.5 A (20 K rise) and 15.5 A (40 K rise); ambient -40 to +125 C with the 40 K Irms; part at most 165 C
   Q2 to Q5 CSD19532Q5B (MAKER, v2/vendor/power/ti-csd19532q5b-n-fet.pdf): RDS(on) 5.7 mOhm maximum at VGS 6 V, 25 C (p.3); RthetaJA 50 C/W maximum on a
     1 in2 2 oz pad (p.3); TJ -55 to 150 C (p.1); Qgd 8.7 nC, Qoss 128 nC at 50 V (p.3); Figure 8 (p.6), the higher of its
     VGS 6 V and 10 V curves, read by pixel
