   MARGIN, the front end's minimum over what passes in service: held -2.203 A (THE FRONT END LIMITS FIRST); proposed +0.378 A
     (CLOSED by CHECK-3 on these inputs; with four FETs switching and U3's pin at CHECK-3's 0.019 A it would read +0.359 A)
   (the energy model's entry E2 carries the printed 6.94 A minimum; the stacked 6.79 A is still above U3, so no energy result
   moves)
   THE TAPS, a condition of every band above: VSNS over R11 alone holds only where R160 and R161 meet R11 at its own pads.
     IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENT (not a defect of the current netlist, which has no layout): the copper R11's current shares with
     the two taps, both sides together, at most 0.371 mOhm at its working temperature: 2.38 mV at 6.415 A, 4.8 % of the 50 mV scale.
     At 25 C (layout extraction, the bench) that is 0.286 mOhm with the copper at 100 C and 0.324 mOhm at 62 C (copper 0.00393 /K,
     INFERRED): the criterion is 0.29 mOhm at 25 C. Verification: (1) the laid board's extraction (dc_drop's mesh, kelvin_check
     on FE_ISNS_P and FE_ISNS_N, declared in pcb_sensitive.yaml) reads at most 0.29 mOhm for the two taps together; kelvin_check's
     own 1 % per tap (0.5 mV of 50 mV at the solved current) is stricter and closes it too; (2) on the bench at 25 C with a
     known current I, the DC voltage across U2 pins 14 and 13 exceeds I x R11 (R11 measured four-wire at its pads) by at most
     0.29 mOhm x I (1.7 mV at 6.0 A)
     HISTORICAL EVIDENCE, revision A32 only (v2/ecad/pcb-a-power-a23/pcb-a-power.kicad_pcb, last commit b7e0d28f of 2026-09-15, routed): U2 pins 13 to 16 sit on VBUS20, FE_OUT, GND, FE_CS,
     the power nets themselves, with no R160, R161, R150 or R151. v2/ecad/pcb-a-power-a23/routed/kelvin_check.verdict.json (2026-09-20, ADVISORY, board sha256/16 58e26c67987b1daa, this file)
     read 26.62 mV of copper drop between R11.1 and U2.14 and 2.16 mV between R11.2 and U2.13 at dc_drop's solved current
     (FE_OUT's declared 6.0 A typical today; pcb_sensitive.yaml's text names 3.80 A): 4.8 to 7.6 mOhm together, both adding to
     the sensed voltage (INFERRED: R11.1 is FE_OUT's only sink, R11.2 VBUS20's only source). It shows how large a tap error has
     been on this board; it is not a reading of the current netlist's board, which does not exist
