       the larger of its 5.7 A and 5.0 A points): 3.47 A matched, 3.49 A at 1.5:1, 4.01 A at 2:1 (124 / 124 / 143 % of 2.8 A): OVER
     copper (track_current.width_for_current, decision 35's conservative model, external, 10 K rise): FE_OUT and VBUS20 9.37 A: 7.2 mm at 1 oz, 3.6 mm at 2 oz; VIN_RAW at 15.1 V 13.94 A: 15.0 mm at 1 oz, 7.5 mm at 2 oz; VIN_RAW at 9.0 V 23.38 A: 38.6 mm at 1 oz, 19.3 mm at 2 oz
   the declarations the generators lay copper and rate parts to: VBUS20 6.0 A typical, 8.0 A peak (gen_sch_a.py);
     VIN_RAW 14.10 A (gen_sch_a.py _VIN_RAW_A, board E's _FE_A: 5.7 A at 20.7 V over 0.93 from 9.0 V); TRK_OUT 10.33 A (gen_sch_e.py)
   against them (INFERRED): VBUS20: held maximum 5.810 A under both; proposed in service 6.415 A PASSES the 6.0 A typical, proposed
     maximum 9.370 A PASSES the 8.0 A peak. VIN_RAW 14.10 A: held at 9.0 V 14.50 A (the stacked band over _FE_A's printed 5.7 A and 20.7 V);
     proposed in service at 9.0 V 16.01 A, at the maximum 23.38 A; _FE_A's own formula at the proposed printed maximum 9.19 A gives
     22.74 A. TRK_OUT 10.33 A: at 15.1 V the proposed in service carries 9.54 A, the maximum 13.94 A
   board E's 200 W stage (Option A(i)'s, NOT DESIGNED: a1elec CHARGER.md 2, 'its owner's'). The front end's input is the stage's
     OUTPUT: 144.1 W in service (6.415 A at 20.887 V over 0.93), 130.5 W at the held maximum, 210.5 W at the proposed maximum. Into
     the stage at its DECLARED 0.93: 154.9, 140.3 and 226.3 W. The model's 200 W is a window on the stage's INPUT (energy_two_pack.py
     node_power: min(panel, window)); the stage has no design, so neither its input nor its output rating is established:
     MISSING EVIDENCE. Where U3 does not limit (a fault) the stage or the array bounds the draw, not R11 (INFERRED)
   the vehicle entry alone: its LM5069 passes at most 6.15 A (gen_sch_e.py _VEH_T), so below 23.4 V a vehicle alone cannot carry
     the proposed in-service 144.1 W (below 21.2 V the held maximum 130.5 W either): the front end's draw on the vehicle is bounded by
     that entry whatever R11 is; the host's IIN_HOST per source is a downstream item (INFERRED)
   VIN_RAW's sources at the proposed maximum: the front end asks 210.5 W; the tracker at 15.1 V would carry 13.94 A against its
     buck current limit 13.8 / 17.2 / 20.4 A (VCS over R5, INFERRED as the average it can pass) and TRK_OUT's declared 10.33 A;
     the vehicle entry passes at most its LM5069's 6.15 A (gen_sch_e.py), under its fuse F1's 8 A at 65 C (gen_sch_e.py, the
     10 A blade derated by pcb_fuse_derating.yaml), whatever R11 is; board E's panel fuse F2 sees the tracker's input,
     210.5 W over its efficiency at the array's 34.3 V set point, about 6.6 A (0.93 DECLARED): under '10 A mini blade'

5. THE LM5176'S OTHER SETTINGS AND R11 (the maker's equations)
   average current limit: ICL(AVG) = 50 mV / RSNS (Eq. 4, p.17): the ONE setting R11 sets; bands in section 3
   the CC loop: its gm amplifier (1 mS, p.7) discharges SS (C7 4.7u) when VSNS passes 50 mV (7.3.6, p.17): the loop's gain
     per ampere scales with R11, so the proposed loop acts at 0.62 of the held loop's gain (INFERRED); its response is a bench item
   the ISNS filter: R160, R161 100 Ohm with C128 1 nF across, Figure 8-1's network ('often used across the ISNS(+) and ISNS(-)
     pins', p.17); the sheet asks for the filter capacitor close to the IC between the pins (p.30). The 100 Ohm ceiling of p.24
     is for the CS and CSG lines (R150, R151 sit at it), not for ISNS (CHECK-3 minor 4). Unchanged by R11. The bias offset is
     0.3 mV either way, 48 mA at the proposed R11 against 30 mA at the held (in section 3's band)
   the current-sense amplifier's range: ISNS common mode 0 to 55 V (p.5) against VBUS20 at most 23.40 V (s120's bound): unchanged;
     ISNS(+) to ISNS(-) is rated +-0.3 V (p.5): at the proposed R11 that is 48 A, far past any current the path can carry
   slope compensation: Eq. 26 (p.24) uses RSENSE, the CS resistor R12, and L1, not R11: CSLOPE = gmSLOPE x L1 / (RSENSE x ACS)
     = 800 pF with 2 uS, 10 uH, 5 mOhm and 5 (the p.24 example's gm and gain), against C147 680p: unchanged by R11. If L1 runs
     near its Isat (section 4) its inductance falls and the dead-beat value falls with it (INFERRED)
   the cycle-by-cycle limits: boost peak 20 / 24 / 28 A and buck valley 13.2 / 16.0 / 18.8 A (VCS over R12 5 mOhm, p.7):
     unchanged; with the average limit raised they, not the average loop, bound L1 at a low VIN_RAW in an overload
   hiccup: MODE to VCC selects no hiccup (p.20), so a sustained overload stays in the average or the cycle-by-cycle limit
     indefinitely: at the proposed R11 it does so at the higher currents of section 4 (the held circuit sat there in service)

